<title>UK: Daimler CFO says currency hedging cut H1 profit.</title>
<headline>Daimler CFO says currency hedging cut H1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG Chief Financial Officer Manfred Gentz said on Thursday group operating profit would have been up to 500 million marks higher if were it not for the company's hedging efforts.</p>
<p>Speaking at a news conference, Gentz said, &quot;Operating profit would have been 400 to 500 million marks higher if we hadn't hedged for currencies.&quot;</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom + 49 228 260 97150</p>
</text>
